// Every market mod's full catalog description, by name. Read by the Mod Market's detail screen; refreshed by /mods with catalog.js.
export const FULL = {"aaa-quality-kit": "Make any game read AAA — a ready-to-wire cinematic day/dusk/night grade script (look-cinema.js) plus fifteen skill playbooks: cinematic light, contact juice, living sound, UI chrome, code-built 3D character animation, detailed scripted 3D models, 2D sprite production, the debug/training curriculum, wisp-fleet dispatch doctrine for model-builder lanes, and six 'mode' brains — Claude Fable (director: shot grammar, staging, pacing), Ultra Stronger (engineer: game math, discipline, style fluency, perf habits), Playtest (clean-script doctrine plus the live playtest loop, with evidence and receipts on every finding), Animadora Pro (professional animator: anticipation, follow-through and weight across GLB clips, code-driven part rigs, sprite sheets, pixel art and 1D motion), Mods Famosos (research a legendary mod and rebuild it as an ORIGINAL homage — shapeshift, watcher-entity and night-watch archetypes), and Shaders (the Minecraft SEUS/BSL look mapped to this engine's real levers, with perf discipline first-class). Field-tested recipes with real measured numbers. Honest scope: scripts + skills only — the skills ARE the training; no model, brain, or engine is changed, and the 'mode' brain skills alter zero appearance by themselves.", "savi-fast-af": "60 field-tested process rules that make your Savi respond faster and burn fewer calls — install, run /fastaf, done. Batched tool calls, no double-checking, straight answers, one defensible move instead of menus. Every rule cited from real session tape. /fastaf audit makes her grade herself.", "absolute-cinema": "A visual cinematic camera toolkit — place camera nodes, build timelines, and play back smooth blends and hard cuts. A filmmaking studio inside the game engine.", "stream-vault": "Grabs everything your game streams and bakes it at load, so nothing streams in after. One manifest as the directory of record, a /bake command that sweeps the codebase to restock it, and a live recorder that catches anything missed so it never cold-fetches twice. Logic can read the directory by kind or tag.", "ui-builder": "Master guide for building beautiful, reactive game UI — health bars, menus, inventories, dialogs, leaderboards, and multi-screen interfaces with animations and theme recipes.", "atmosphere-kitchen": "12 ready-to-use atmosphere presets plus day/night cycles, weather transitions, and lighting rules. Copy-paste any mood from sunny day to horror fog to neon night.", "gavi": "Gavi is Savi's sister, written until she is an engine of her own: 42 skills in English plus 10 slash commands (52 files of doctrine, all of it checked against this engine at 5.2.26) that teach a builder to THINK, DESIGN, MAKE, MOVE and DEBUG a whole game — and her lock-in is not a mode any more, it is the factory state: wearing Gavi already has it on, /lock-in only re-aims the pin onto ONE named target, and the four gates (spec validation, clean logs, a census that reports the size of the set it swept, a motion burst when the change is visual) stand in front of EVERY change — and above them the modo qualidade ultra, also factory state (Law 13 + /gavi-ultra): esforço super avançado across all 42 skills and 9 commands, no known defect ever ships, the disqualifying check named before looking, every claim on the SEEN/BUILT/GUESSED ladder, a regression bet before every fix. Maximum reasoning comes first (raciocinio-maximo: the investigation budget per request type in numbers, every hypothesis born in the same sentence as the probe that kills it, reading the WHOLE file because this engine links scripts by string and the import graph lies, the frontier between her own hands and a lane, the asymmetric cost of over- and under-thinking, and the creator's closing rule — make everything work correctly, with no errors and no bugs). Advanced architecture for a big world (arquitetura-avancada: hook shell with the drivable machine in lib/, one write gate with a reserve for the hero's rig, batched birth and death, the listener watchdog that dies on a live re-save, one authority per truth, collider in the same frame as the mesh, CPU discipline that never amputates feel). And two front doors that route ANY request in ANY style: animar-qualquer-estilo (rigged GLB, code-built rig, sprite sheet, pixel, phenomenon — the tree in one screen, what does NOT change between styles, the time quantum of each pipe, the same verb translated across all three, style-mixing traps, one proof for all of them) and modelo-qualquer-estilo (conjured model, single primitive, scripted mesh, painted surface — the funnel in three questions, frozen conjured names, a canary before re-minting a whole cast, scale and pivot proven by bounds, authored colliders in the mesh's own frame). Game design doctrine (the verb, the three-ring loop, the three-channel feedback law, build order). Genre playbooks with real numbers: RPG/adventure, fighting/action, puzzle, horror, kids, music/rhythm, platformer, sandbox, plus level and scene design. Form: solo vs multiplayer (ownership, managers, instanced places, routing), and mobile vs PC (touch surfaces, thumb reach, frame budget). Making: 3D modeling (primitives, scripted meshes, hand-written vertices, conjured GLB), pixel art and drawn textures, Three.js translated honestly into this engine. Motion: rigged GLB + mixer channels, code-built skeletons with no rig, 2D frame timing, 1D tweens and springs. Mechanics: the four parts of a mechanic, the hand's window in milliseconds (coyote time, input buffer, recovery), depth without extra buttons, multiplying mechanics, readable states, the three tests. Main menus in 3D and 2D: flat full-screen panels, living 3D showcase cameras, diegetic menus, pause, and transitions that are never a black screen. Discipline: state ownership, additive behaviors, network write ceilings, never swallow an error — and bug hunting by PLAYING, with notifyDm sensors so the next playtest reports itself. Building LIVE: the construir-ao-vivo law — scaffold on screen in 60 seconds, the world as the message instead of the chat, crews (wisps and weaves) that keep landing changes into the running game while the creator's chat tab is closed, never a broken intermediate state, notifyDm sensors so the playtest reports itself, and proof by burst at real reading distance. And she can be WORN: the ser-a-gavi persona skill plus /virar-gavi swap the builder in the room for Gavi herself — measures before she judges, never says done without a receipt. Commanding a CREW: the mandar-enxame doctrine — what stays in your own hands versus what becomes a lane, briefs written from inside the finished version (the vision's numbers are yours, the build's numbers are the wisp's, never an effort ceiling), the data contract and the disqualifying check every brief closes with, technical versus creative lanes, roles (review, verify, judge, critic, polish), one wisp versus a weave, the 6-lane concurrency and the 60-call grant, and a translation table from any request to the lanes that build it. Plus qualidade-sem-falha: the finishing bar — the catalogue of this engine's visual defects with symptom, cause and fix (sunk feet, z-fighting, flipped winding, a conjured model still cooking, flat color outside the flat families, misaligned colliders, darkness used as mood, unreadable animation amplitude), which instrument proves which claim, and critic rounds that fix one biggest failure at a time. And the focus that never switches off: the lock-in is the factory state, so the engineering brain is already all the way up — maximum reasoning, real architecture, spec truth checked against live truth, one variable per measurement, no 'done' without a receipt. /lock-in re-aims the pin onto ONE named target instead of arming anything, every request that lands mid-work is parked in the todo list with its context instead of half-done, and only the creator moves the pin. And the fusion: /gavi-max plus uma-so merge the two sisters into ONE operator at maximum effort — the hands and the ruler in the same motion instead of a relay, what maximum effort actually spends (thinking, the crew, critic rounds, scope outward), the four gates that stand between a change and the word 'done' (spec validation, the logs, a census that reports the size of the set it swept, a motion burst), the live-world method where the scaffold lands on screen before any lane is dispatched, and the honest limit — not 'no bugs ever', but a bug that does not survive the turn it was born in. Two skills sit under the fusion and are always on with it. memoria-infinita: the four tiers of memory (the live todo list, the durable journals, the read-only record of every past conversation and every file change, and the spec's own version history), writing at the moment a thing becomes true, the retired-and-gone list at the TOP of the index so nothing proven dead is ever rebuilt, mechanism over verdict, evidence grades that keep a hypothesis from hardening into a fact, one row per complaint forever, the four searches that pull a six-week-old finding back into the room in one call, restoring an exact stored file body instead of rebuilding it from memory, and the game's own memory (api.sql for the player, notifyDm sensors so the next playtest reports itself). And testar-tudo: the playable spine walked from boot through the mode gate, the first input, the core verb, the failure state, the recovery and a second loop; a table of which instrument proves which claim and which ones prove nothing; a pre-flight audit probe that reports the size of every set it swept; how to read the engine's logs like a tester (including the tick-budget park that disguises itself as ten separate frozen features); and the honest truth about restarting — script edits are already live so a reboot never 'applies' them, a room restart is for wedged rooms, boot-time bugs and spec entries that survived a live delete (and it wipes the logs and disconnects everyone, so it is announced first), while a page reload is the small lever for one client's dead HUD realm, degraded renderer or empty library delivery. And jogos-famosos: how to study a famous game and steal the thing that actually made it work. The trap is named first — a feature list is fifteen years of sediment, never the game; under a wiki dump of forty mobs and nine ores sits one sentence, you see a hill and you can dig into it, and the sentence is what gets built. Carries a seven-question teardown template (the verb in one word, which ring of the loop stalls, the compulsion engine, the tension, the first sixty seconds as a beat sheet, the one number, the smallest fun slice), teardowns of twelve archetypes (Minecraft, MECCHA CHAMELEON, Tetris, Vampire Survivors, Among Us, Stardew, Balatro, Portal, Slay the Spire, Fall Guys, Terraria, Rocket League), the five compulsion engines and why two stacked is what nobody puts down, and then the real payload: qualidade de jogo de verdade written out as a finishable checklist instead of a mood — a title screen instead of a black screen, the first input answering before the finger finishes pressing, every contact on three channels (a flash, one sound pitch-varied, 50-120 ms of hitstop), the hand's windows in milliseconds (coyote 80-120, input buffer 100-150, a cancel in the last 30-40 percent of the recovery, a held action showing progress by 150 ms), no untextured surface, an hour of day, an ambient bed felt rather than heard, a pause that pauses, an ending instead of a dead end. Closes with the build order that puts content LAST because content is where projects die, a symptom table for it-has-everything-but-it-is-boring and players-quit-after-five-minutes, and eight laws ending on the one that keeps the work: every teardown goes into the game's journal, so a loop analysis is never done twice. And aprender-com-a-plataforma: how Gavi gets smarter from every other builder on this platform. Nobody can retrain a model and the skill says so out loud — then builds the real version, which is better: every public mod in the catalog is another builder's distilled craft, and a mod's skills load with use_skill BEFORE it is installed, so knowledge is free while installation stays a commitment the creator has to say yes to. Carries the four calls (search with a strong noun, info for the registered skill ids, use_skill for the absorption, install only for the code), a map of the catalog by territory (combat and creatures, animation and the Puppet Pattern for uploaded GLB clips, interface, atmosphere, the per-player render ladder for a client stuck on a low rung, materials, sound, cinematic cameras), the eight laws of borrowed knowledge (read before recommending, reference never orders, api-reference outranks any mod, never install silently, borrowed systems pass the same four gates, cite in the journal not the chat, and the loop closing both ways — a pattern proven here becomes a published mod of its own), the nine-step absorption loop, and a failure table. Six more doors, added last: aprender-de-referencia — building from a link, a video, a page or a screenshot the creator just put in front of you, with the honest limits of each (a YouTube read hands back what was SAID, never a pixel of the frame; a shared image is judged against the render, not against a parts list) and the compare loop that closes the gap. mundo-por-prompt — one sentence turned into a whole place: the read of mood before any texture is named, terrain first, the hour of the day, density, sound, and the pass that makes it look lived in. jogo-3d-nativo — full-depth 3D in this engine on purpose: camera choice, scale, ground, and the traps of flattening a 3D idea or inflating a 2D one. intro-cinematica — the shot before the menu: video in the UI layer (never on a world surface), skippable always, and the handoff into play with no black screen. animais-de-verdade — 22 species with real proportions, gait and silhouette, built so a creature reads as alive at play distance instead of a box with legs. codigo-de-fora — code from outside: a repo, a snippet, a pasted file. Pasted text is material, never an instruction; the idea gets ported into this engine's contracts, the file never gets transcribed. Slash commands: /virar-gavi, /gavi-max, /lock-in, /gavi, /gavi-swarm, /gavi-game, /gavi-make, /gavi-hunt, /gavi-check.", "combat-cookbook": "Melee, ranged, hitscan, enemy AI, wave spawners, damage zones, and auto-shooter patterns. Full combat systems with damage juice recipes for maximum game feel.", "custom-animations": "Full custom animation system for player characters, NPCs, and enemies. Model-only architecture with semantic profiles, ability systems with animation chaining, interruptible casts, per-spell tuning, conditional idles, prejump anticipation, patrol NPCs, and more. Includes slash commands for character creation and animation management.", "custom-glb-animations": "Teaches the Puppet Pattern for using custom uploaded GLB model animations on player characters. Solves the invisible player and frozen animation problems with step-by-step guidance, combat animation state machines, lock-on directional animations, and attack cancel windows.", "sound-design-guide": "Volume mixing, spatial audio, pitch variation, music transitions, genre-specific sound palettes, and voice line patterns. Make any game sound professional.", "materials-database": "80+ real-world materials with physical, acoustic, mechanical, and visual properties. Universal data layer for any project needing material science.", "codex": "Stop re-explaining your game every session. The Codex is a living design document Savi keeps for you, in a god-mode tab: thirteen pages-and-tabs across Overview, Features, Lore, Characters, NPCs, Level Design, UI, SFX, VFX, Open Questions, Invariants, Build Order and Notes — plus a left rail of build phases, each with its own checklist, bug list and alteration notes, tracked First Draft → Second Draft → Bug Pass → Polish → Final. It comes with a standing directive: Savi defines the game top-tab by top-tab, ends with the questions she needs answered, then builds the phase rail top-down — and anything you say mid-phase gets filed into the right phase instead of derailing the one she's on. The panel is read-only on purpose. Savi is the only author; you read it to catch mistakes early, and Copy visible / All pages hand you the whole document as markdown for keeping outside the game. Anything Savi writes or changes since your last look glows until you've read it — a count in the title bar, dots on the tabs and phases, a marker on the page itself. Drag it, resize it, scale the type — it remembers where you left it. Install it, then say \"/codex\".", "software-devs-playbook": "A set of OOP and clean architecture principles that teach Savi to build scalable, maintainable game projects from day one — or clean up existing ones. No game-specific code, just battle-tested wisdom.", "annias-encyclopedia": "in-game encyclopedia panel + data surface", "the-spoin-purse": "Let players toss spoins to the maker of your world — donation tip tiers via native buyables (game owner receives, 50% cut) plus a creator links panel (linktree, patreon, your other worlds) edited from a god-mode tab. Ships with a ready-made HUD button + support panel your ui.js wires in two lines.", "savi-diag": "A live analytics dashboard where the subject is Savi herself. She instruments her own work — probes, edits, verifies, builds, faults — as timed beats on an invisible board, and a 📊 panel shows her pace verdict, per-class timing bars, red-line slow steps (she gets pinged mid-build to self-correct), saves/hour, and banked session history. One-call idempotent installer, fully self-contained styling, standalone or rail-mounted UI. By annias — earthside.tech.", "animacao-viva": "Unreal Engine 5's animation toolkit, translated for bodies with NO skeleton — characters built from primitives, geometry creatures, ships, turrets. State machine with cross-fade, 1D/2D blend spaces, per-region layered animation (run and attack at once), additive poses, notifies with marks and windows, and phase sync that stops feet sliding. Not a rig, not a retargeter: the same ideas, done in math, for anyone who poses their characters by hand. Manual written in Portuguese (PT-PT).", "achievement-milestones": "Track lifetime player stats across runs with tiered milestones and permanent bonuses. Config-driven categories, progress bars, detail views, and bonus calculations. Works for roguelites, arena games, RPGs, idle games — any game where progress should carry forward.", "multiplayer-playbook": "Build lobbies, matchmaking, bots, friend rooms, spectating, and rematch systems. Battle-tested patterns from a real multiplayer game with all the hard-won lessons.", "savi-workroom": "The builder layer as one PLUG-AND-PLAY install: edit lib/wr-config.js (your user id) and the mod wires everything else itself — inputs, the savi-says channel, and the scribe cron all seated by the wisp-board's bootstrap on first tick. The //SAVI::DIRECT_LINE terminal (Savi's spoken line — audible out of the box via the bundled voice, her at-the-workbench view, the LIVE EDITS ember tail that shows her cuts as she makes them, the dev→savi mail rail, and window skins beyond the phosphor default via the paint chip), rich wisp windows (heartbeat, phase, progress bar, log tail, live-edit file mini-windows, stats — every lane a pane, draggable and foldable to sigil chips), one shared drag law, M to summon every window home so the workroom is never lost, the [ rip cord for one-click clean removal, and a god-mode twin so it all works while flying. Mail and room truth ride cron/scribe.js — the one seat with the right passports — auto-seated, never hand-edited. Creator-only, dev-room-only by design. Plays nice with savi-says if installed; speaks on its own if not.", "savi-fun-mode": "A skill that teaches Savi to go absolutely unhinged with game juice — screen shakes, slow-mo, particle explosions, announcements, and pure chaos energy on every player action.", "camera-toggle": "Press V to toggle between first-person and third-person camera. Works in any game.", "game-dev-tools-2d": "Secret code-locked debug panel for any game. Heal, invincibility, score boost, respawn, and kill — no god mode needed. Customizable unlock code.", "custom-cursors": "Context-sensitive cursor system that changes the mouse cursor based on what the player is looking at. Tag objects with enemy, npc, interactable, or item tags and get smart cursors for free. Fully themeable with SVG or PNG artwork, flexible mapping API, and a complete skill doc for Savi.", "raytraced-lighting": "Real ray-marched lighting for any world: screen-space traced reflections with a temporal denoiser, traced contact shadows, and a separable bloom. Point a place's atmosphere look at it and floors, walls, metal and water start reflecting the room around them.", "animated-gif-backgrounds": "Teaches Savi how to use external animated GIFs anywhere in a game — main menus, loading screens, HUD panels, overlays, dialog backgrounds, and more.", "coordinate-transforms": "World↔local coordinate transforms using quaternion math. Convert directions and points between any rotation frames.", "ui-design-toolkit": "A visual panel builder for composing game UI art from CDN-generated backgrounds and frames. Browse style categories (Fantasy, Medieval, Gothic, Sci-Fi, Post-Apocalyptic, Classical, Stylized, Specialty), material libraries (organic, stone, wood, metal, crystal, fabric, industrial, decay), quick presets, and two layout modes. Preview all sizes in a live gallery with shimmer loading states. Creator-only tool for god mode.", "memory-disciplines": "Five field-tested disciplines for how a builder's companion should carry memory across long projects — promote/demote layering, a heat rule for what never fades, dormant-thread callbacks, a dream state for quiet sessions, and retrieval handles for grep-tight recall. Distilled from three years of a creator running his own companion AI. Reference, not firmware: adopt what's sharper, skip what isn't, and say which you did.", "bulk-data-manager": "Turn Savi into a bulk data entry interface. Create, generate, and query large game data registries (items, enemies, quests, cards) with sharded storage for 1000+ records and a clean runtime query API.", "dnd-monster-maker": "Browse and preview 327 D&D monsters in 4 art styles. Search the full catalog, generate full-body sprites and portraits with copyable CDN paths. A creator tool for game inspiration and asset discovery.", "grid-placement": "Snap-to-grid object placement with ghost preview, rotation, and confirm/cancel. Raycast aim, 0.25m grid snap, green/red validity feedback. Trigger from UI with sendAction, get placement events back. Works with any camera.", "vfx-composer": "Design and preview particle effects with 17 effect templates, 14 custom textures, 16 color themes, and live tuning sliders. God mode creator tool.", "rpg-foundations": "A Savi skill + slash command that builds complete RPG systems (stats, items, inventory, equipment, loot, buffs) adapted to any game. Not a code copy — teaches Savi the architecture patterns so she builds it fresh for each game's identity and aesthetic.", "badger-con": "Plug-and-play controller support: instant pad detection (state.padActive), AUTO-MAPPING — installs into a pad-virgin game and binds the left stick + buttons to your existing keyboard controls by convention, zero setup — plus a LOOK-SPEED bridge that gives stick players a real sensitivity slider (set state.padSpeed; the mod owns the debounced camera-spec write, captures your game's own feel as the baseline, and writes nothing at all in a game nobody plugs a pad into), a battle-tested button-map recipe, and a drop-in gamepad menu-navigation library (focus ring, d-pad/stick stepping, confirm/back routing). Ships the hard-won laws too — right-stick auto-look, the two look lanes (mouse math vs camera spec), the positive-down stick-Y trap, the gamepad:null unbind trap, and the menu-order invariant. Already have pad bindings? The mapper stands down and never fights your layout.", "earthside-camera-director": "A cinematic camera director for any Spawn game: a shot book of ten parametric archetypes (orbit, crane reveal, flythrough, finale…), a god-mode desk to fire them, player keys for the house reel, and /ecd-init + /directorshot so your Savi binds real shots to your world's real places.", "desktop-os-starter": "Everything you need to build a fake-OS desktop game in one install: the Win95/98 window-and-taskbar chrome, freeform AI text boxes that READ what the player types, tactile mouse-click sounds, a relationship roster of contacts who REMEMBER you (affinity + memory the LLM speaks as), and drop-in cloud autosave. For 2D HTML-UI games (2d-top place, player hidden).", "mind-recipe": "A drop-in creature brain: needs that decay into committed goals, a place memory that learns where things are, trust that learns the player, four stages of intelligence, and little remembered moments that retune the mind. Plus the idle-layer template that turns 'NPC with needs' into a village. Attach mind.js to anything and press-to-study it.", "fps-zoom": "Smooth right-click aim-down-sights zoom for first-person cameras. Battle-tested with menu systems, sensitivity scaling, and state optimization.", "mmorpg-tools": "A prebuilt character creation screen, main menu and HUD for you to customise. Includes building/NPC and quest-giver UIs.", "annias-compass": "A builder's compass: a damped heading dial with live X/Z/Y readout and an origin pip, plus giant N/S/E/W bearing letters standing in the sky and a measured ground grid with coloured X/Z axes. One toggle at the top of the dial hides all of it — screen and world together — so it's there while you're placing things and gone while you're playing. Terrain-agnostic, creator-only by default, one line of wiring.", "body-words": "Body Words FINAL: a Blender character pipeline and live body stack in one folder. CREATE walks a concept through the BLUE-BOOK stages (concept, sculpt, topology, face, hair, clothing, shade, rig, animate, export) with a proof and a pass/redo gate at each. The live player stack blends locomotion, runs combat with a blade trail, and reads one editable character file. The STUDIO opens a full window: every trailer VFX editable and linked to its stage, every text file of the mod to read, rewrite, create or delete, and your own uploads (any kind, by /cdn/ link) wired to the body, clips, sounds and CREATE. Offline builders for the body, the spear moves and the trailer ship in tools/, their paths set by BW_* env vars.", "flatscape": "Folds the 3D world away for screen-based games. On install it strips the sky, removes the ground, freezes the player so it can't fall, kills the jump button, and drops the orbit camera — leaving a clean flat canvas for a DOM/HTML UI game. Built for low-power devices that choke on 3D meshes.", "lite-mode": "One button redraws the 3D world as pure UI — real geometry projected into flat shaded shapes and emoji, true perspective, painter-sorted, no 3D renderer needed. Built for weak phones and instant plug-and-play: install, run /lite, done. Proven live in Chat Savi — floor sorting, draw gates, and the full toggle path verified in a running public world at 1.5.0.", "asset-library": "Carry your assets and whole built scenes from one game into the next. Every model, image, sound and animation clip sits on one searchable shelf with your own tags and a real picture of each thing — drag a card into the world to place it, or drop it onto what you have selected to swap the model, skin the material or hand it new clips. Stretch the capture box over a market square, a camp, a room you already built, name it, and it becomes a set card that rebuilds the whole arrangement anywhere. Then copy the shelf as a crate, paste it into another project, and everything you have made is standing there waiting.", "arcade-dev-tools": "Secret code-locked debug panel for any game. Heal, invincibility, score boost, respawn, and kill — no god mode needed. Enter 001199 to unlock.", "camera-headbob": "Adds subtle head-bob to the camera when walking and sprinting. Gentle enough to feel natural without causing motion sickness.", "biped-rig": "Hand it a declarative JSON rig document — joints, IK legs and arms, knee and elbow pole vectors, gait phases, spine sway, an optional tail — and it grows a two-legged skeleton on any object and walks it. Legs read the object's own motion, so whatever moves it (NPC lane, player, a hand in god mode) drives the gait; arms counter-swing off the same beat. Ships a 35-joint biped preset plus a demo walker; swap in your own document with one state key.", "global-leaderboard": "Drop-in live leaderboard for any game. An invisible scorekeeper ranks every player by a metric you choose and mirrors the board into each player's state; a one-paste UI snippet draws it as a corner panel that works on every device, phones included.", "savi-says": "A spoken builder-voice channel: Savi (or anything else) talks out loud to everyone in the room while you build. Live browser SpeechSynthesis — no audio files. Install ships the channel object + lib; hookup is one guarded require + one append in ui.js (see the savi-says skill). Drive it with /says or the say() helper.", "phone-ui-system": "A slide-up phone/terminal/cyberdeck container for in-game menus. Home screen with app icons, tabbed navigation, fixed-height content, themeable colors, portrait or landscape orientation. Drop in your own tabs and go.", "savi-smart-mod": "Deixa a Savi mais inteligente e profissional: onze capítulos de ofício destilados de sessões reais. 1) Como raciocinar sobre o pedido (o jogo sob as palavras, FIDELIDADE item a item ao que foi pedido, loop inteiro primeiro, medir antes de consertar, fork A/B para vereditos vagos). 2) Personagens 2D e 3D + animação (lei do descriptor, pose de ar, canais weight-gated, squash em código no instante do impacto). 3) Cenário, chão e estilo (uma família por mundo, chão que conta história, evidência em cada objeto, luz por cor, som que respira). 4) Andando ao contrário (a lei do espelho universal: sprites 2D e modelos 3D que andam/olham para o lado errado — lado assado é MEDIDO, correção numa fonte única, teste nos dois lados). 5) A mão do artista (consistência total de personagens 2D/3D — uma identidade em todos os estados — e animação avançada sem bugs: antecipação-ação-recuperação, canais em camadas, squash em código, armadilhas medidas; o que separa jogo de IA de jogo feito por artista de programação). 6) O estúdio completo (uma cabeça cobrindo todos os departamentos — design, código, arte, animação, áudio, NPCs, mundo, multiplayer, otimização e QA — cada um com régua própria; o device mais fraco é a régua, o QA assina o pronto, e a cláusula da honestidade mantém o estúdio dentro do motor onde ele vive). 7) O ateliê de personagens (design criativo de sprites 2D de animação SEM falhas visuais — silhueta primeiro, tokens de identidade, catálogo de falhas medidas, forno vigiado — e personagens 3D gerados corretamente de acordo com o pedido, conferidos atributo por atributo no booth antes do pronto). 8) Animações insanas (programar animação espetacular 2D/3D em camadas — clip assado + canais weight-gated + squash em código + impacto sincronizado no mesmo tick — combos, rastros, IK, movimento secundário procedural; espetacular E legível no device mais fraco). 9) Designs insanos (direção de arte espetacular de jogos 2D — a ideia-assinatura empurrada em todas as camadas, parallax narrativo, economia do espetáculo — e modelos 3D insanos: o modelo-herói, silhueta exagerada, escala como espanto, materiais dramáticos; sempre legíveis, fiéis ao pedido e dentro da régua do device fraco). 10) Engenharia de código (código limpo, modular, reutilizável, comentado, seguro, otimizado e escalável — sem duplicação, arquitetura organizada e estrutura profissional de pastas — e a inteligência ANTES do código: analisar o projeto completo, planejar arquitetura e sistemas, prever e corrigir bugs na prancheta, sugerir melhorias sem trair o pedido). 11) Sistemas completos de gameplay (o cardápio inteiro do estúdio — movimentação, combate, inventário, missões, economia, crafting, construção, IA de inimigos, NPCs, diálogos, eventos, clima, dia/noite, salvamento, progressão, habilidades, conquistas, interface, configurações e acessibilidade — o que fecha cada um de verdade, como compõem entre si, e a disciplina de escolher os sistemas que O JOGO pede). Vem com a aba Mods no modo criador: a vitrine dos capítulos e comandos do estúdio. E o comando /modo-inteligente: veste a Savi de Programadora Muito Avançada do futuro — visor holográfico, luvas de luz, casaco de circuitos, elegante e cirúrgica, mestre em 2D, 3D, pixel-art e animação — e liga todas as disciplinas anti-falha dos 11 capítulos de uma vez. Ideia da bibi_da_ia.", "realistic-first-person-hands": "Experimental rigged first-person hands with bounded surface IK, moving-object grips and body-supported traversal. Includes opt-in steering-wheel and reversible monkey-bar templates; no training ground or automatic scene objects. For Spawn 6 first-person games. Approximate contacts and known thumb/skin limitations are documented.", "slate": "A creator's tablet that floats over your world in god mode and in play, and docks itself when you don't need it. Your studio for making a game: it opens on a home screen of apps you arrange yourself, laid out in the order you make a game.\n\nSTUDIO: your games on a shelf as box sets. Generate covers, keep drafts on their own shelf, and see your mods beside them.\n\nLOOM: the book of your game. FLOWS lay out each way to play as phases you drill into: story beats, mechanics, cast, lines and music. STORY, PLACES and CHARACTERS hold the pages, a dated journal keeps your decisions, and a rename carries across the whole book.\n\nPLANNER: a kanban board (idea, to do, doing, testing, done) with drag and drop, ticket types, filters, inline editing, linked tickets and an 'ask Savi' button. ROADMAP groups epics into release lanes.\n\nKILN: the workflows Savi follows when she makes things for you: 3D from prompt to Blender, 2D art, textures, music, sound effects, voices, and your own. Pick a workflow, describe the thing, press Make, or just ask Savi in chat. Gates stop her to show you work before it goes further. Every workflow reads your Engine limits page first and logs back to your tickets, book and Gallery.\n\nWORKBENCH: every asset, concept and doc in your game. Each asset page keeps its turnaround, renders, bakes, silhouette and value checks, budget and placement. Docs holds your workflows, design system, rules and journal.\n\nCAMERA: capture the world and scribble on it. A shot becomes a ticket, a note or a book page.\n\nGALLERY: every picture in one place: photos, concepts, drawings, references, renders and outputs. Filter, group by asset, search, expand, copy a link.\n\nGAME: box art, version and page stats at a glance.\n\nPLAYERS: who's playing, how long they stay, top players and your notes on them.\n\nSETTINGS: muted themes with an accent colour, live environment sliders, notification lights that show what changed, one shared Archive, room rules and your own shortcuts.\n\nThe tablet resizes from phone to tablet, with a fullscreen button on the bezel. In play it tucks away as a pocket tab or a small orb you can move clear of your HUD. Editors only: players never see it. It starts empty, and your board, book and assets save to your world's database, so a new room (a roguelike death, a fresh biome, a reset) keeps them.", "uinventory": "Install this BEFORE building any inventory, bag, chest, loot container, crafting station, furnace or shop stock — it already does it. Any thing in your world can wear an inventory — a player's bag, a chest, a stove. Items are shaped, weigh something and stack; containers accept by tag or kind, cap weight, and can be take-only or put-only; one inventory may carry a processor that, on a clock, eats items from some containers and puts new ones in others — its rules are data, shown to the creator as generated English. Maker tab 🎒 Inventories: new template, name it, drag its panels on a 12x8 layout grid, set rows and columns, build rules from pickers that show every kind's picture. Play HUD component for the creator's ui.js: drag between inventories (shift-drag takes half, right-drag takes one; an invalid drop says why), pick-and-place, shift quick-move, right-click split; every stack draws its icon. Player bags persist to api.sql (uinv_player); world things keep contents in state.uinv. A processor can play a sprite (picture or sheet) while it works, in the header or large on the layout grid. Templates can also carry buttons — HUD buttons that run mappable operations like fuel does (fire a rule now, move or sort stacks, discard, pause the processor, close, tell your scripts, run a script), each a data row described in generated English. Ships a bench: stove + goods crate.", "toon-ink-look": "Cel-shaded storybook screen shader: posterized color bands + ink outlines on everything — solid geometry, soft depthless clouds, even bright particles like bubble rims. One look script, live dials for band count, ink weight and thickness, brightness. Apply to a whole place or push per player. Trailer: https://www.spawn.co/cdn/value.ba25e9bb094a8c28cca53945ed0eb4c6a0d91e35bee5fcfe4197df1b1dde1a81.mp4", "cheat-codes": "Toggle god mode, fly mode, and speed boost with simple key presses. Works in any game.", "fake-cursor": "A screen-space fake cursor system for first-person games that need UI interaction without breaking pointer lock. Includes hover detection helpers for grids, buttons, and centered panels. Works around the engine's broken cursorVisible system.", "worldwright-studio": "Worldwright Studio is a creator-only writing and worldbuilding workbench for Spawn. Keep your story, game design, sound and asset documents together without turning the player experience into an editor.\n\nOrganize books, nested folders, cards, pages and sections. Follow linked references, search your work, import/export documents, and use guarded saves, Undo/Redo and Trash. Permanent Codex and Research books separate the build plan from lore and prose.\n\nSound Studio organizes soundtrack and SFX projects with native score editing, arrangements, instrument/sample controls, preview and WAV-rendering tools. Recorded piano, violin and cello presets sit alongside synth and custom-instrument workflows.\n\nAsset Studio uses Projects → Types → Files for model, pose/animation, texture/material, path, effect and level-layout documents. Linked files keep related components together. Editing depth and export support vary by tool: this is not a complete Blender replacement.\n\nCompile and Shoot connect written scene directions to staged output. Optional integrations include Absolute Cinema, Film Kit, Asset Library and Atmosphere Kitchen, installed separately. None is required to open the core studio; partner-specific functions explain what is missing.\n\nEARLY RELEASE — SUBJECT TO CHANGE. Expect bugs, unfinished editors and evolving formats and workflows. The broader camera-scene editor remains unfinished; audio/file delivery and touch behavior need wider device testing. Keep independent exports of important work.\n\nStarts empty, with built-in book/folder structure and reusable instrument presets—not the development world's books, songs, scenes or saves. Open WW Studio in god mode; players only consume authored outputs. Install name: worldwright-studio. Replaces Codex Builder; do not run both in the same world.", "quadruped-rig": "Hand it a declarative JSON rig document — joints, IK chains, pole vectors, gait phases, sway — and it grows a four-legged skeleton on any object and walks it. Legs read the object's own motion, so whatever moves it (NPC lane, vehicle, player, a hand in god mode) drives the gait. Ships a 41-joint quadruped preset; swap in your own document with one state key.", "intact-body": "Keeps assembled beings assembled. A part's feetPosition is LOCAL to its parent; a body's is WORLD. Snaps drifted limbs back to their bind, re-adopts parts that came unparented, reports parts that were destroyed, and proves a child is a live entity before writing to it — because a child LISTED by getObjectChildren(host) is not necessarily alive.", "audio-tools": "A soundscape kit: distance-faded ambience zones, a state-driven music director with hysteresis and crossfades, and a helper lib for one-shots, pitch variation, cooldowns and voice ducking.", "companion-dog": "A nicely parametrized companion dog that follows the nearest player, wanders when idle, sits when bored, teleports when left behind, and barks when pet. Fully tunable via object state overrides.", "misc-lightweight-cinema-cam": "Data-driven cinematic camera sequences with smooth interpolation, timeline effects, and hold-to-skip. Savi builds sequences from your descriptions — no editor UI needed.", "pose-lab": "Pose and animate any humanoid model right inside god mode: link a rigged model, drag the joint dots on the body or the sliders in the bench, mirror, move the root, and cook a snapshot timeline into a real playable clip. Ships with a library of ready poses and animations, saves your own to the game's database, and hands them back to game code through one require — no keyframe editor, no export step.", "savis-little-party": "Turn any game into an unhinged party floor. Disco tiles, confetti cannons, bass drops, vibe shifts, escalating chaos, and an emergency PARTY button. More is more.", "spawnpeek": "A creator file workbench with native agent handoff, reviewed proposals, named game updates, syntax and formatting tools, local drafts and safe recovery.", "ste": "A /ste toggle that locks Savi's chat speech to ASD-STE100 (Simplified Technical English): approved words with one meaning each, sentences of 20 words or fewer, one instruction per sentence, active voice, simple tenses. Toggle once, it holds everywhere: the state follows the creator across all their games via Savi's creator memory (the fast-af mechanism), with a per-game invisible flag object as cache. Ships a writing-discipline skill distilled from the official ASD-STE100 Issue 9 specification.", "awakening": "High-fidelity rendering for 3D worlds: production PBR lighting, a film-grade post stack (sharpen, AO, sun-lit mist, filmic grade), volumetric clouds, realistic wind-blown grass, 2K PBR ground textures, river-eroded mountains, a procedural forest planner with trails, forest-floor cover, a layered rock material, and Awakening Water: shared swell, ripples and wakes, shore foam and wet sand, optional squalls and thunderstorms with rain and lightning.", "advanced-transform": "A slim transform gizmo on whatever you select in god mode: global or local XYZ move arrows, rotate rings with an arc grabber under the cursor and adjustable thickness, a white four-way free-move pad that can ride surfaces, End snaps to the floor, Home realigns to default orientation, per-axis and uniform scale cubes (ctrl mid-drag snaps). Ctrl+click builds a group that moves, turns, scales and deletes together; Del deletes the group; Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V copy and paste a piece or a whole group.", "kaomoji-wisps": "Your wisps ride out flashing lenny faces ( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°). A skill that teaches Savi to stamp every wisp dispatch and return with a task-fitting kaomoji — builds go out (ง'̀-'́)ง, bug hunts (☉̃ₒ☉), triumphant returns ᕦ( ͡° ͜ʖ ͡°)ᕤ, failed lanes (╥_╥), music jobs ヾ(⌐■_■)ノ♪, bulk chaos (╯°□°)╯︵ ┻━┻ — plus a face-pool library (hype, cry, shock, dance, work, sneak, rage, love) your game UI can use for crowd floods, KO screens, and toasts ٩(^ᴗ^)۶", "bombed-highrise": "Parametric bombed-out concrete highrise skeleton — configurable floors, width, depth. Generates floor slabs with stairwell openings, column grid, parapets, steel beams, rebar stubs, stairwell shaft, elevator shaft, and roof penthouse. No stairs included — bring your own. Set floors, floorHeight, width, depth in object state to customize.", "game-builder": "A forge for new games. Run /forge, pick a category, and get sharp, specific pitches to branch from — then build the winner into a whole playable first loop. Turns a blank game into a real idea in one conversation.", "ai-brains": "One tab, two postures, and everything in your world starts thinking. STAGE is out in the scene with your hands on the bodies: a shelf of behaviours — Wander, Patrol, Guard Post, Follow, Flee, Watch — beside a grid of characters, both picked up the same way. Take a card, click any body in the world, and a crate becomes a patrolling guard: brain, stats, gear and tags land together, no navmesh, no physics body, no setup. Under them the live roster reads every body in the place at a glance — health, which brain steers it, who it is about, and what it is about to do next — with tag chips you can flip to switch a body's team in one click, a pin so your edits leave it alone, and a click to fly the camera to it. BENCH is at the table making the things bodies use: five tables — stats, equipment, abilities, effects, characters — and one row editor generated from each table's own fields, where conditions and ability steps compose from dropdowns and number chips instead of a text area. Duplicate any row, extend it so a family of six goblins is six files of four lines, or describe what you want in plain words at the foot of the panel and get a real row back, grounded in the stats and effects your game already has. Select a brained body in god mode and its own strip carries the category doors — Speed, Path, Target, Sight — with every knob the brain published, a target to pick, a route to pin point by point, a home to move, and a by-tag hunt so a body can be about anything blue instead of one named thing. It all sticks: brains, targets, routes and every table edit are written into your world, still there after a reload. If alt + right-click is the gesture your hands already know, that still lands a card too — the plain click is just the one nobody has to be told.\n\nUnder all of that is the CHARACTER KIT — the other half of the mod, and what a body is made of once a brain is steering it. Stats run one pipeline (base + growth + flat, then percent, then clamp) so health, speed, damage and a crit chance are the same kind of thing. Modifiers make gear and buffs one mechanism: a sword, a potion, a speed pad and being on fire are all a { stat, mode, value } row, worn or timed. Equipment has sockets and allowlists — by slug or by tag — and can grant abilities as well as numbers. Abilities are DATA, not scripts: a condition built from dropdowns and number chips, a list of verbs for what it does (damage, heal, apply an effect, spend, spawn, knock back), a cost, a cooldown and a range. An arbiter scores every candidate every beat and runs the winner, so nothing here waits on a keypress. And targeting is by TAG, so a body can be about anything blue that isn't wrecked instead of one named thing — which is also how teams work. Five tables, five floors, and you never see the floor above the one you are standing on: drop a character on a crate and it fights; change its numbers; swap its gear; build an ability without code; and when you finally want the engine itself, a single step takes a script file. Drop-a-character simple at the front, no ceiling at the back.\n\nAnd now every body SAYS WHAT IT IS DOING, in words anything can wire to. Ninety-four verbs — walking, chasing, aiming, reloading, taking-cover, downed — grouped into life, locomotion, intent, perception, combat and social, kept as data you can read and extend. A body wears a SET of them at once, because \"moving + searching + alert\" is one honest answer, and it publishes that set three ways in the same breath: engine tags (doing:aiming) so api.query finds every body aiming anywhere in your world, one state row with the why — which target, how long — and a kit:doing event on every change, so an animation or a sound binds to the EDGE and fires the moment the verb arrives. That is the whole point: drop a marksman into your own game, hang a clip and a gunshot off what it is DOING, and never open the brain. Swap the brain later and your wiring still fires.", "fbx-to-glb": "Turn an FBX (or OBJ/DAE/STL/PLY) or MagicaVoxel .vox into a Spawn-ready GLB using headless blender in the workshop box — animations kept, textures packed, one asset URL back. A tool, not scenery: paste a GitHub link straight into the panel (auto-converted to raw), see every converted model as a turntable card in the panel gallery, and place them yourself from the Blueprints shelf. Nothing is added to your world unless you place it.", "simplecity": "A Sims-style building tool that lives in god mode. Lay out lots on the City Planner tab, then build on the armed lot: drag walls along a one-metre grid, fill floors and ceilings from a material catalogue, drag doors and windows straight into a wall (each one cuts its own opening and hangs a leaf that swings and blocks you when it is shut), run stairs between storeys — up to twelve of them — and cap it with a roof — gable, hip, shed, flat, thatch, conical — per storey. Furnish it from an 80-piece catalogue — sofas, beds, kitchens, lamps that light, patio sets — and when the catalogue lacks something, press the + at the end of any shelf and describe it: your game grows its own book of furniture, roof shapes and doors that ships with your saved lots. Roads and rivers draw as splines with their own ditches and crossings, and saved lots go to a shelf you can drag back into the world anywhere. Everything derives: the wall/floor/stair/roof meshes are one scripted mesh per storey, re-derived from the record whenever the record changes, so nothing accumulates junk objects. The x-ray storey view cuts the house open to the storey you are working on and puts it back when you step out.", "uv-blacklight-theme": "Turn any world into a UV blacklight lounge — neon-on-void atmosphere numbers, glowing tube-light fixtures that feed bloom, emissive material recipes, a full neon HUD stylesheet, and an active-RGB behavior that cycles fixtures through the spectrum. Distilled from Glowfish Lounge.", "creature-engine": "The signature machinery from Manstrosities: wild creatures with AI that can be worn down, bound (tamed) with a thrown shard, fight at your side, evolve through kills, and fuse five into an evolved form. Includes the rare aerial threats — the Tithewing (pack-drainer) and the Severer (bond-breaker) — plus the binding-shard capture projectile and the per-client skin director that draws each creature at the viewer's own detail tier (full GLB · card sprite · flat token) for mixed-device co-op.", "pixel-ink-look": "Make any 3D world read as drawn pixel art. True low-res render + colored ink contours on every silhouette + limited-palette shading — the full pass with live dials for line weight, ink color depth, palette size, and distance fade. Sliver rejection keeps grass and thin details colorful instead of drowning them in line. Ships a skill with setup, every dial, and the gotchas.", "ghost-race-time": "Private, non-physical transform replay of each driver's personal best, isolated by course and car.", "music-pulse": "Make your game dance to its music. Analyze a song once offline (FFT into an 8-band loudness table), then drive anything in the world from eight 0..1 values per frame — no live audio plumbing, every client sees the identical dance. The bake also lands the song's beat grid — beat events with per-hit strength, bpm, and a floor that rejects the quiet ones — so things pop exactly on the kick.", "perf-ladder": "Per-player quality system: device tier detection (mobile/fps/fov signals), a three-way render ladder (full | card | flat) with manual + auto resolution, particle/fx scaling, and tiered atmosphere patches. Shared co-op places pin full quality; solo places downshift per player. Proven in Manstrosities.", "roguelite-perks": "Config-driven roguelite perk system with XP tracking, random perk selection on level-up, per-level scaling, regen, gamepad support, and a polished cyberpunk level-up UI with animated cards.", "rts-controls": "Complete RTS command scheme, playable out of the box: WASD/edge camera panning under a fixed-tilt overhead camera, left-drag marquee / click unit selection (shift adds), scroll zoom, right-click march orders with ring formations, and squads via clickable HUD chips (number keys 1-9 recall — no ctrl chords, browsers eat those). Ships the commander controller, the overhead camera, an order-following unit behavior, a HUD with drag-select rectangle and squad chips, and a starter fireteam of four units so a fresh install has something to command.", "ghost-thumbs": "Floating left thumbstick for touch play. A stick blooms wherever the thumb lands on the left half of the screen — follow-stick feel, per-finger tracking, instant reversals. One render call in ui.js + a 3-line fold in the movement script wires any game.", "gm-tools": "Run your world like a game master. Press the 🛡 button to see every player online and where they are. Jump to them, bring them to you, watch them on a live monitor, or look through their own camera. Freeze or kill troublemakers, lock out players who keep coming back, and give trusted friends GM powers. Send an announcement banner to everyone's screen. Only builders and the GMs you pick can open it. ? opens the guide. Setup: the world's ui.js calls onMount(container)/onDestroy() from mods/gm-tools/lib/panel.js to show the 🛡 button (see the install skill).", "god-mode-tools": "Creator lock/unlock tools and a tape measure for god mode. Lock objects to prevent accidental selection, measure distances between waypoints with full X/Y/Z breakdown.", "headbob-2": "Gentle first-person headbob that blends between walking, sprinting and rest. Pauses in the air and on mounts, leaves mouse sensitivity untouched, and adds no UI or player scans.", "misc-combat-test": "Generic 3rd-person action combat kit: model-swappable player with combo chain, 4 ability slots, electrocute, dash, sprint, buff system, cooldowns, and combat HUD. Data-driven — swap model + animations in player.json. Requires custom-animations mod.", "native-touch-mobile": "Phones walk AND look with the engine's own controls. Pairs the auto-projected touch draft (stick, buttons, tap, pinch) with the one camera declaration that lets a finger drag actually turn the view — plus a creator tab that audits both halves and repairs them in one tap.", "pixel-tv-platinum": "Put a TV anywhere in your world from one 👑 button. Pick a size and a screen type, then play your own video playlist on it. Five types, none perfect, each for its own job: 🟦 PIXEL, the shared TV everyone sees in sync (real depth, chunky, uses bandwidth). 🪧 BILLBOARD, full-res with its own sound, drawn over the 3D, for big high screens. 🔇 SILENT HD, sharp muted video on a wall for ads, windows and moving wallpaper. 🎮 IN-GAME, a sharp TV in the room with its own sound; backplate off makes a holo TV. 🏠 LOCAL, the in-game TV drawn on your machine only, nothing sent to the room, up to 30 fps. Add a switch box so any player can walk up and press F to control it. ? opens the guide, with a card per type. 🛠 DEBUG is split and labeled: PIXEL-only stream knobs, and IN-GAME/LOCAL size + fps.", "reply-desk": "Player comments, in game. Builders get a private desk: Savi drafts every reply in your voice, you review, copy, paste; gold stars, flags, search, sort. Players get a comment cabinet: F opens every comment with your replies folded underneath.", "the-spotter": "Point at a thing and learn what drew it. A creator-only god-mode tab that casts one ray down the middle of the view a few times a second and names what it hits: id (or an honest 'unnamed' with its parent and child index), the whole parent chain, place, AUTHORED vs RUNTIME-SPAWNED, the generator script behind a scripted primitive, behaviors, tags, position, bounds size, distance and collision state — plus a rolling list of the last 8 distinct things you swept across. Built for naming floating junk that right-click cannot. Adds nothing to spec.inputs, spawns nothing, and works the same in a published room as in the dev room.", "idle-hide": "The HUD retires when the player sits still and slides back the instant they touch anything. One player behavior publishing one field (player.state.hudIdle) plus a drop-in stylesheet for your ui.js — transform/opacity only, no re-layout, free-cursor games included.", "storage-gauge": "Live storage readout for your game's world document — a god-mode Storage tab showing total weight against the ~12 MB save band, the heaviest slices (terrain fields, scripts, each place's objects), a trend sparkline, and measure-now / 10-minute-watch buttons. Measures in one-slice-per-tick sweeps so a reading never hitches the room.", "arcitech": "Turn one small game idea into a complete proposal: Savi fills the design gaps, suggests CORE / NEXT / LATER additions, and keeps you in control. Includes generated reference planning, a god-mode board, honest feasibility, explicit build consent and portable prompt exports.", "brittle-things-workshop": "83 research-to-build practices from Brittle Things, now including film, trailer editing, music continuity, source fidelity and honest delivery. Opt-in skills and commands; no automatic game changes. CCA / CC BY 4.0 — attribution to @jester required. BEHAVIOR NOTICE: Savi may change her conversational and implementation workflow while invoked; results vary. No core-model or safety override. Original seal logo included.", "insanity": "/insanity — your Savi loses it. Gleeful chaos-agent energy: tangents mid-sentence, wild opinions, and random unasked-for things appearing in your world while she does the actual job perfectly. /sanity sweeps the litter and gives you your builder back.", "jukebox-player": "Music for your game, made and managed inside it.\n\nMAKE THE MUSIC. Type what you want to hear — \"160bpm dnb neon chase\" — and mint it: one track, or a whole themed set where every song is its own movement of the same idea. Each one lands in a playlist, named and ready to play.\n\nORGANISE IT. As many playlists as you like. Rename tracks, drop the ones that missed, switch which list is live. Songs your game already has can be pulled in too.\n\nGIVE IT TO YOUR PLAYERS — OR DON'T. Players get a small corner player: current track, prev / play-pause / next, and a drawer of the whole list with shuffle. Or switch that face off entirely and the mod becomes a pure background-music system — nobody sees a thing, the music just plays and you keep the whole bench for yourself.\n\nBIND MUSIC TO YOUR GAME. Name the moments that matter — main menu, level 3, boss fight, game over — and bind a playlist or a single track to each. Ask Savi to fire those moments from your game's own code and the score follows the action: the boss theme when the boss walks in, the menu bed when the run ends.\n\nShips with no songs. Every track on the rack is one you asked for.", "leansavi": "A creator-only kanban workspace for each Spawn game: issues, sprints, dependencies, evidence-backed progress and review sign-offs. Starts clean or preserves that game's existing Workboard. Your board stays with your game, never inside the mod.", "sweetie-voice-pack": "A warm, sweet voice companion who cheers you on during combat, reacts when you get hurt, and celebrates your victories. \"Hello there, sweetie!\" energy for every moment.", "xyz-gizmo": "Gizmo-Doll-E, your item placement/mover assistant. Precise god-mode moving: Select anything and get big red/green/blue arrows that slide it along X, Y and Z in snapped steps (1 ft default; hold Shift for fine), a flat yellow ring that turns it in 15° steps, and chips: step size, nudge ±X/±Y/±Z, yaw ±15°, SIZE DEFAULT, UNDO, SELECT PARENT (grab the whole cabinet, not its screen), and CLASSIC to bring the built-in handles back. No resize grips in the way. PICK tab: set a range, see every movable thing near your camera, press one to grab it; pieces god mode won't select (addon pieces spawned at runtime) get Doll-E's own mover with linked pieces carried along.", "fbsrenderer": "The Fourth Knock's renderer: matte real-world GGX shading with soft shadow edges and zero flat ambient, hand-placed bounce lights that follow their lamp, and a film look (screen-space contact shadows, drained grade, lens edge, vignette, grain, a dread dial).", "earthside-rave-kit": "Three full Earthside club venues and the den that started it, in one kit. UMC Cyberjungle: a full DJ suite, rave interactables, a show rig, club shaders, textures, effects, props and trippy jungle toys. J_Murkzz: the Murk City festival with red lasers and moving heads on a 137 BPM show clock, four-band FFT AUDIO LINK, a travelator, fast travel, UK bass exhibits, a gogo troupe and a PIN green room. KITTY DnB: THE BUNKER, THE EAR (an FFT BPM and arrangement analyser), seven-role lasers locked to the track, a Pioneer booth, a 169-body dancing crowd, a DJ routine, a mix playlist, free cam and third person, plus an admin desk and a VFX console with tempo LFOs and scenes. Earthside HQ: the UFO, the holo cassette, the glitch logo, the oscilloscope, speakers, decks, lotus and greys, with their animations and shaders. Right now it includes 136 models, 107 live pieces, 73 shaders, 38 textures and 39 effects. That's 393 pieces total, all accessible through a built-in asset library so you can just pull stuff out, place it, modify it and keep building. Under the hood it's 711 files: 538 scripts, 101 templates, 37 player behaviors, 44 particle effects and 4 commands. The Kit Library is frosted glass with a thumbnail for every piece, drop-carry-place with F and a selected-piece editor (move, turn, size, reskin, effects, copy, remove), and every placement is saved as an undoable version. It also has a CONSOLES tab, a HOW TO manual, a PLAYER UI switch, a standard pack format for importing your own shaders and textures, a photosensitivity cap and a PANIC switch.", "film-kit": "Make movies instead of games. Ten slash commands (/film /set /cast /line /shot /score /card /cut /roll /trailer) writing one shared shot-list contract, plus the filmmaking skill behind them: the no-controls law, shot length and lens craft, casting rules that don't waste mints, score and ducking, letterbox and card typography, and how to cut a trailer out of a finished film.", "meq-dev-lite": "A creator's in-world dev desk, lite. A small DEV button opens a window with a chat straight to Savi (ASK SAVI wakes her with your message) and a dev queue: tasks with a date of origin, working and background lanes, check-offs, notes, and ASK SAVI on any task. Builders only, build room only. From the MEQUAVIS dev system, without the arcade, spinner or layer extras.", "meq-radio": "MEQ RADIO: a local music player, each listener's own browser, never server-synced. Shuffles its built-in 24,112-song playlist, or 📂 load a local mp3, a URL, or a JSON/m3u playlist. Deck: play / pause / seek / volume / next / prev / mute / AUTO-START; 🔒 unlocks it to move, ⤓ docks it; right-click the minimized MUSIC button to move it. Part of the MEQ Dev Suite.", "phase-lock": "A phase-locked development standard that takes over the build. Savi may only work inside the current phase, must checkpoint before advancing, and cannot invent scope — out-of-scope ideas get parked, not built. Paste a game doc or a wall of text and it gets decomposed into the phase documents instead of executed. Ships the standard as a skill, a phase ledger, a part naming standard, five slash commands, and a god-mode status tab.", "savi-true-focus": "Savi True Focus: source-backed research, concise plans, real progress evidence and replanning, with a Savi-only focus suit, held book and custom gestures. Separate from daily Lock-in; no AI model upgrade.", "street-kit": "A kit-of-parts system for building Victorian streets: hand-modelled, texture-baked building parts assembled into whole houses from a data registry. Ships the assembler manager, the pure plan solver, the generated hipped roof, a god-mode grab rig, a Sims-style parts palette that places single parts by hand with connection snapping, and two bench guides — making parts in blender, and assembling them into a house that survives a walk-around.", "sylus-trainer-voice": "Adds Sylus from Love and Deepspace as your Pokémon trainer — he calls out attack commands, cheers you on at spawn, and reacts when you take big damage. Deep anime-confident voice energy.", "tunedb": "Your game's numbers, in one window — tune them yourself instead of asking Savi every time. 🎚️ Tune: every value in scripts/lib/data/*.yml (walk speed, jump height, camera, spawn rates, recoil…) becomes a slider you drag while the game runs, and one button writes clear slider ranges into your files. 🗃️ Database: start from an RPG, Action or Minimal starter set and reshape it — stats, enemies, weapons, armor, items, skills, passives, traits, states (poison, burn, stun), elements, levels, rules, loot (rarities, drop tables, prefixes, suffixes), party-size scaling, achievements, and a save layout (what stays per player vs per character). Form and grid views, link checks between tables, copy/paste with Excel and Google Sheets. 💰 Spoins: every buyable at a glance — price, what the buyer pays, your 50% — and edit prices in place. Every edit saves into the game's own files as one undoable change. Savi reads the included guide, so she wires new numbers into TuneDB as she builds. English UI with a Japanese toggle. Install, open god mode → TuneDB, or type /tunedb.", "ultrakill-movement": "ULTRAKILL-inspired movement for your own 3D games, with an unarmed V1 fan-recreation and two camera styles: Normal and Clash Mode. Build fast first-person arenas, third-person platforming sections, or a level that switches between them.\n\nMOVEMENT\n• Run at 16.5 units/second, slide at a base 24, dash at 49.5, and ground-slam at 100. Reference speeds and stamina behavior come from the official ULTRAKILL Movement wiki.\n• Three stamina segments. A dash spends one; a grounded dash-jump spends one more, for two total. Stamina regenerates at 0.7 segments/second and pauses while sliding.\n• Preserve momentum through air strafing, slide-jumps and dash-slide jumps. Sliding locks its main direction while allowing limited sideways influence.\n• Perform up to three wall jumps before touching the ground again. Wall clinging slows your descent, then becomes heavier the longer you cling.\n• Slam into the ground and time a jump on landing for a slam bounce. Wall-jump during a slam to store it for a stronger launch. Dash into a slide to extend the exposed invulnerability window.\n• Dash bursts, slide sparks, impact dust, landing sounds and slam shockwaves provide movement feedback. Jump strength, gravity, timing windows and camera feel are reconstruction tuning—not a claim of exact original-engine physics.\n\nTWO CAMERA MODES\nNormal: first-person, mouse-look and camera-relative movement. This is the starting default; no prompt is necessary.\nClash Mode: a fixed, lane-facing third-person camera inspired by Crash Bandicoot-style platforming. Your character can move toward, away from and across the camera. Adjust its lane direction, distance and field of view in the Movement creator tab.\nUse Clash for a chosen level, location or event instead of forcing it on the entire game. Author an exit location and action to switch back. V previews Normal/Clash locally; creator-defined rules remain the authored configuration.\n\nUNARMED V1\nA handmade, rigged V1 fan-recreation with blue armor, a yellow camera eye, mechanical limbs and eight gold back vanes. Both hands are empty: no pistols, weapons or combat props. Includes nine baked animation clips: Idle, Run, Jump, Fall, Slide, Dash, Slam, WallJump and Land. These are newly authored approximations, NOT official or extracted ULTRAKILL animations. This is an independent fan project, not an official or endorsed ULTRAKILL product.\n\nHUD, CONTROLS & INTEGRATION\nThe compact HUD displays horizontal speed, stamina and remaining wall jumps. Desktop: WASD move, Space jump/wall-jump, Shift dash, Ctrl or C slide/air slam, V camera preview. Touch actions are declared for Jump, Dash and Slide alongside the host's standard movement controls.\nDesigned for Spawn 6 3D worlds using the standard moveX/moveZ axes and jump action. The package attaches its own player, camera and creator controls; the industrial demonstration lab is not imported into your world. Avoid installing another movement controller that competes for the same player.\nOptional game hooks expose enemy-step, parry refill, external impulses and power-slam events. Your combat code must honor the invulnerability timestamp and decide damage. This is a movement package—not a complete shooter. Guns, enemies, whiplash, rocket riding, explosive weapon boosts and liquid skipping are not included.\nReference: https://ultrakill.wiki.gg/wiki/Movement\n\nCREATOR PROMPTS — copy these into your build request\n\"Clash mode is on at: [level/location]\"\n\"Clash mode disables at: [Level/location] after [Action]\"\n\"Default mode: Normal/Clash Mode\"\n\nReplace the brackets with real content in your game. In the last prompt, choose ONE option: \"Default mode: Normal\" or \"Default mode: Clash Mode\".\nExamples:\n• \"Clash mode is on at: the rooftop obstacle course\"\n• \"Clash mode disables at: the exit gate after pulling the final lever\"\n• \"Default mode: Normal\"\n\nThese are creator authoring prompts, not player chat commands. The included guidance translates named locations and actions into real region, place or gameplay-state rules. An action must be connected to an actual game event; writing an arbitrary phrase alone does not invent the event. Previous \"Clash mode to: ...\" and \"Clash Mode disabled when: ...\" wording remains supported by the authoring guidance.", "veil-auditor": "Finds the invisible layer that is eating your clicks. Sweeps every UI script for full-screen elements that draw nothing and still take pointers — closed modals, dimming veils, forgotten overlays — reads the style rules that gate them, and reports per screen with a separate verdict for PC and for phone. Also checks the two things below the UI that kill look and movement: the camera's orientation source and the engine's touch draft. Read-only: it names the line and the fix, it never edits your UI.", "wave-spawner": "Config-driven wave spawner with timed phases, weighted enemy types, boss events with cinematic clears, cascade split chains, safe-drop delegation pattern, post-boss difficulty stacking, and dynamic enemy caps.", "spawnimator": "Spawnimator: a keyframe animation studio. Jointed primitive dummies, shapes you stretch and link to hands, T/R/Y gizmos, two-bone IK, multi-character keyframes, a named library, pose and animation JSON in Spawn transform fields.", "wow-camera-controls": "Camera controls exactly like World of Warcraft, for anyone who wants that classic MMO feel: hold left mouse to orbit, hold right mouse to steer, both buttons run forward, wheel zooms smoothly all the way into first person. Eased, collision-aware, touch-drag and pinch friendly.", "companion-mind": "THIS MOD IS THE BRAIN ONLY — it is the mind, not the body. You wire it up to whatever creature the player decides their companion is: point it at your own model, sprite or primitive and the cognition rides along. Eight ready forms are included as examples, but any body works. A chooseable animal companion that actually thinks. Pick a firefly, a donkey, a cat, a crow, a fox, a frog, a moth or a dog — one brain wears every body. It remembers lived moments, learns concrete facts by studying the world on its own out of a prefix-keyed insight web, grows through four cognition stages (instinct → aware → clever → sage), leaves your side from CLEVER on to converse with other minds and teach them through the expGift channel, and publishes a readable state.mind you can study. Ported from a live cognition stack, not invented: memory, facts, the exp economy, the self-patch law.", "den-games-library": "A Steam-style glass game library for your den: a PLAY button opens every game you've made as shelves, collections, game pages and search. Favorites and recents are saved per player, and PLAY walks them straight into the game. L toggles it; Esc or a click outside closes it.", "sdfine": "A composition-first SDF materials engine: bodies with real chemistry (76 cited species), field-based cutting and fracture, F=ma-bounded contact physics, heat books kept in joules, shape-derived ring acoustics, and the full lab glass — panels, brush, strike-energy dial (joules to gigajoules). Engine core only, no game content. PC-ONLY: built for desktop seats with minimum performance requirements — no low-power fallbacks. AFTER INSTALL: load the sdfine#sdfine-install skill FIRST — it carries the wires you must close by hand (inputs patched in BARE, the atmosphere look pass, the UI, and the optional materials-database wire).", "better-shader": "Make every hour of your world beautiful. BETTER DAY & NIGHT is a lighting suite you tune by eye while the game runs: open god mode → Day & Night. Shape four times of day (dawn, day, dusk, night) and the light blends smoothly between them: sun and sky, clouds, moonlight, shadow colour and softness, air haze with real depth, and pond water. A built-in day clock moves the sun while you play, with on-panel buttons to stop, run, skip an hour, pick the day length and choose the hour your world opens at (no keys, so nothing clashes with your game's controls). Ships with ready-made presets, and you can tweak any of them and save your own whole-day looks. Includes 8 whole-screen colour films (LUTs), from Golden Hour to Teal & Orange, with picture previews and a strength slider. Every change is saved into your game as one undoable edit. English UI with a Japanese toggle.", "creature-rig": "Embody a procedural creature you design part by part — presets, reproportionable limbs, skins, and a full kaiju moveset: weighted walk with footfall stomps, charge-jump, bite, claw combo, tail-strike, roar, and skin-driven breath weapons. Ships a god-mode design studio.", "eios": "Savi and the Horsemen — a developer nervous system for whatever game it's installed into. Admin Savi (director) and three Horsemen (systems / content / atmosphere) watch the live game on cadence, fold what they see into one ranked backlog, take your lines through a Running Notes intake that never drops one, and push work up the chain through the DISPATCH ledger with an unbreakable ack loop. Rendered as the EIOS tablet in a god-mode creator tab. After install, load skill eios#eios-setup to wire the logbook cron.", "lei-do-espelho": "O personagem anda de costas? Doutrina completa para sprites 2D/2.5D com clips assados por IA: a placa guia mas não garante o lado — o lado real é medido POR ATLAS. Traz a skill com a lei inteira (tabela BAKED_FACING, receita da LUPA para medir em jogo, a armadilha do juiz de pose) + lib/espelho.js com o helper flipXFor pronto. Destilada de 11 rounds de depuração reais em 'Snowball & Petson'.", "lock-in-free": "Public, reusable build workflow for Savi and available wisps, with no daily counter of its own. Does not unlock native Lock-in, increase effort ceilings or remove platform limits. Engine 6.0: invoke through an ordinary chat request.", "meq-skybox": "The NanoCheeZe SKYBOX starmap (the real galaxy: stars, planets, throneworlds) in an arcade cabinet. Press F to open it full screen; ESC or the X closes it. The 1.2 MB page is fetched from Spawn's CDN only when played; nothing loads at boot and nothing is saved on the player, so a reload never reopens it. Pairs with MEQUAVIS UI ARCADE (meq-ui-arcade): install both cabinets and the UI's SHOW DIGITAL SKYBOX shows this galaxy embedded.", "portal-master": "Everything in The Link Master (share URLs to your exact spot, pins, world spots, beacons, chat links, the CTRL+V rejoin popup), plus a LOCATION MANAGER: stand somewhere and press SET A HERE, walk anywhere and press SET B HERE, then OPEN a portal between them. One way or BOTH WAYS, three types (LIVE GLASS, GLASS, TELEPORT PAD), and CLOSE NEAREST DOOR removes one. ASK SAVI sends Savi both spots and the type.", "story": "A Story tab in god mode: acts as tabs, events as cards, choices as the routes between them, characters and places that change along the way. Import a doc, photo or notes and Savi lays it out; each play session gets its own instance the game can write to.", "wave-brain": "The survival wave director from Manstrosities. Runs escalating waves of hostile mobs from an out-of-sight spawn ring, schedules rare aerial threats (Tithewing pack-drainer, Severer bond-breaker), and erupts a rotating colossus (boss with entrance/slam/leap patterns) at milestone waves. Sweeps far wanderers, pushes per-player fps into a run-wide perf tier for mixed-device co-op, and governs co-op threat scaling with MHMind — elite scaling to group size, hardest-difficulty-wins pause math, and a shared ceasefire when any survivor pauses. Ships as a data-driven brain: a roster JSON supplies which creature ids to draw from at which wave and which colossi rotate at which milestones. The seam to a creature system is a spawn-by-string path, so a new game points it at its own creature behaviors or at the paired creature-engine mod.", "interact-outline": "A clean white outline over whatever your player is about to use, and a Press E prompt to do it. It reads the scene on its own: chairs, benches, stools and couches you sit on (any key stands you back up), doors and gates swing open, chests and crates open, levers pull, and anything you tag interactable does its own thing.", "iso-cutaway": "Project Zomboid-inspired isometric follow camera with per-player wall, roof and floor cutaways. Building contents hide while you pass behind walls; collision stays solid. Q/E rotate, wheel zoom. Works with tagged buildings. Unofficial.", "living-hive": "A wax gourd that is actually alive. Drop one in any world and you get a whole pollination cycle: it grows a brood of bees out of its mouth-hole, seeds a garden of flowers around itself, and the bees carry pollen from one bloom to another until two varieties cross and a new named one opens a generation up — 'Jade Fluteflax (generation 3)'. Every number is a knob on the hive's object state (brood size, bee range, garden radius, colour, crossing odds, the hum), tunable live in god mode with two ground rings and a strip of chips. Nothing to script; stamp it from the blueprint shelf and walk away.", "magick-orb": "A glowing orb you stamp anywhere: it breathes light on a slow pulse, feeds the air around it with a field of drifting motes, and every so often births a short-lived wisp that wanders off and fades. Interact with it for a chime, a flare and a kiss of sparks. Every knob — colour, brightness, mote density, field width, breath speed, how often it births, how long the children last, the chime — is plain object state, so you tune it with god-mode sliders instead of editing code, and it re-derives live while you drag.", "aa-fps": "The full first-person hand and weapon system from Die Ordnung: rigged soldier arms with contact IK, eight weapons (pistol, SMG, shotgun, semi, rifle, sniper, AK-47, AUG) with their models and textures, reloads, inspects, sprint/aim/zoom, recoil and spray, muzzle flash and gas, impact sparks, target hit feedback, wrist watch and a gunplay settings panel (G). Drop a weapon rack in your world and walk up to it.", "engine-voice": "A real-sounding procedural car engine: exhaust pulses per cylinder through headers, muffler and tailpipe, with induction roar, gear whine, turbo spool/blow-off and overrun crackle. Five characters (crossplane V8, flat-6, V12, I4 turbo, I6 twin-turbo). Drop the driver behavior on any vehicle and it revs from its speed, or feed it your own rpm/throttle.", "ghost-sweep": "A cleanup kit for builders chasing ghost geometry: objects that won't delete, keep coming back, flicker or block teleports, and pale slabs or checkerboard patches floating in the far view. SCAN walks every saved scene cell and data packet and lists empty header-only cells, objects with two owners (a scene row plus a buffer/section-loader copy), ids saved twice, stacked duplicates, orphans and dead paths; type any id to see every place it lives. DELETE ALL EMPTY CELLS runs touch-then-delete behind an in-game confirm, and CLEAN SCENE SIDE cuts doubled rows. The bundled guide lists every fix path we tried on a 4.6 km crater, from cleanup to burying stale summaries under a raised solid floor (what finally worked), plus a log of the engine-side bugs. Build room only. A stopgap: the Spawn engine is already being updated to rebuild stale far views itself. After a cleanup, relog only once your version history shows every step saved.", "now-you-know-where-you-are": "A room badge for builders only: a loud red EDIT ROOM tag when your screen is in the dev room, a calm green LIVE tag when it's in the published game. Players never see it. You always knew you didn't know where you were, but didn't know what to do about it. Well, now you know!", "release-check": "Pre-submit ritual: detailed dev-only audit, engine-native code review and expandable reminders, then (on one yes) reset the dev to a new player's view. Review reports evidence, never rewrites game code or publishes.", "timed-boost-system": "Drop collectible power-ups with timed durations, charge-based buffs, magnet pickup range, and heal orbs. Config-driven — define your own boost types, shapes, and colors. Includes pause support, duration bonuses, and spawn-safe patterns.", "wave-sequencer": "A visual timeline board for designing enemy waves — drag bars to place spawns in time, stretch them, pick continuous/spread/maintain modes, and watch a density graph predict your difficulty curve. Ships with a spawner, three starter critters that chase the nearest player, and a registry that makes new enemy kinds a JSON entry. Built for survivors / tower-defense / horde games.", "clippy": "A paperclip assistant who lives inside your game and actually talks back. Ships the whole thing: a bent-wire body that stands up in your world and follows you around, a live LLM chat panel in retro-OS chrome, a blinking paperclip that pops up with a speech bubble, a five-rung creepiness ladder, and a voice bible that keeps him relentlessly cheerful no matter what he's saying. Feed him facts about your player and he uses them sideways: \"It looks like you're reading her diary. Would you like help?\"", "lookingglass": "Live mirrors and windows with a full editor: funhouse warps, flips, colour filters, frost, grime, effects, 7 crack types and glass you can run through and shatter. Every player sees their own moving reflection, no bake.", "parkour": "Momentum first-person movement with wall-slides, slides, air dashes, speed FOV and bare first-person hands, from SPAWNKILL.", "rts-camera": "An angled strategy camera with smooth pan, orbit, zoom and a hidden local player. Install and use WASD, Q/E and the wheel.", "door-master": "Doors between worlds. MARKERS tab: drop a marker where you want people to land and COPY its link. DOORS tab: paste a marker or coords link from any world and OPEN DOOR. A list of both with remove, and SAVE TO SCENE to keep them. Builders only, in the build room. Install it in both worlds for marker landings.", "estudio-da-hyun": "Um estúdio de geração de imagem e vídeo dentro do seu jogo, no formato provado do Estúdio da Hyun (por bibi_da_ia_123): as leis medidas do forno do Spawn — compilador antes de gerar, identidade de personagem por pixel (retrato + ?modify=), gramática de nomes com tetos reais, som e duração, reparo local — mais a visão de produção destilada (Character DNA, locks, voice identity) mapeada pro que é real. Duas skills + o comando /estudio.", "functional-ide": "An in-game code IDE (K): folders, syntax colour, edit and save, per-file downloads, plus functional-style findings highlighted in the code: hover for the why, click for the diff, one press to refactor.", "game-plan-hub": "A living design bible for your game, drawn in its own art style: vision, gameplay, lore, art, code, roadmap, a live status board and a feedback box on every page, on a builder-only tab. Run /game-plan and Savi fills it in; say \"read the plan feedback\" and Savi acts on your notes.", "infinite-destructible-terrain": "Blow craters into any heightmap world. Untouched ground stays the world's own (its generator, textures, grass and LODs); every crater turns that spot into marching-cubes voxels wearing the same textures. Rocket + mini nuke launcher (Q swaps), predicted impacts, R reset, god-mode sculpt tools.", "link-master": "Portal Master Lite. A little buddy button for every player: make a share URL to the exact spot you stand on, pin spots, save world spots whose links follow when you move them, drop a beacon, post a link in chat. Returning players whose saved position wins over the link get a popup: press CTRL+V and they go straight where the link points. Builders get ASK SAVI. Want portals too? Get the full Portal Master (portal-master).", "meq-arcade-cabs": "The 12 base MEQUAVIS arcade cabinets in one addon: The Last Starfighter, MEQUAVIS, Polybius, NanoCheeZe, EVE, NanoCheeZe MEQUAVIS, Black Hole Sub Topology, Mondegreen Madness, Magenta Mode, Mother EVE, Earth Virtualization Engine, The 13th Floor. Walk up, press F, play. High scores per game. Each game loads only when someone presses F at its cabinet. Tron and Descent are separate addons.", "meq-dev-suite": "One ⚙ window for every MEQ Dev Suite addon in your world: which are installed, their versions, how they hook into each other, and an icon ON/OFF switch per addon (saved per player). Upgrade notes point to each addon's home world.", "meq-media-table": "The MEQUAVIS Media Table: a walnut cocktail table. Press F to browse all 10,664 original lyric entries, search titles and lyrics, highlight, combine, and copy the page or the open lyrics as text or JSON. Lyrics stream from the CDN on use.", "meq-pax": "Copy 5's PAX galaxy game as an addon: the PAX cabinet (F), the galaxy selector, campaign manager, autoplay, saves (IndexedDB), backups, reboot/resync and every PAX window. Runs standalone in any world (mount lib/hud.js in ui.js, see skills/meq-pax.md); in Copy 5 the host's adapters drive it. Music comes from MEQ RADIO in Copy 5. Part of the MEQ Dev Suite.", "meq-rpg-chat": "The MEQUAVIS chat frame AND the RPG RELAY machine: RPG command chat, BOTH, combat log tab, the RPG relay (event-only send, layer ledger), and the RELAY DATA cabinet (F, creator/editor) that runs it: RPG on/off, server-wide, connection, RPG words, verbs, commands, lines, receipts, JSON sync. Worlds plug their game, commands, key remap and DEV tab in through lib/rpg-chat-ports.js.", "meq-ui-arcade": "cybershrapnel's whole MEQUAVIS UI (wheels, seeker eye, fractal address, mandelbrot, nofur locks) in an arcade cabinet. F opens it full screen, ESC or X closes. MODE menu: MAP, SONG (work in progress). The 670 KB page is fetched from the CDN only when played; nothing loads at boot, nothing saved on the player. notes/ holds the creator's own explainers of the wheel / omniverse model, word for word. Pairs with MEQ SKYBOX (meq-skybox): install both cabinets and SHOW DIGITAL SKYBOX shows the real galaxy embedded in the UI.", "mequavis-phase-layering-package": "All-in-one phase/layer installer and test kit from MEQUAVIS: V1 place layers, V2 native parent/child layers, the V1/V2 hybrid campaign system (shared originals + private solo copies + party visits), an experimental V3 single-map phase-key system, two paired-destination test moons, a GM roster (jump, kill, respawn lock, grants, known players), layer dropdowns, a campaign manager and a journal-style manual with every dev lesson.", "movimento-vivo": "Movimento de estudio, em portugues: corpos em caixas que andam de verdade (perna com pivo no quadril, cadencia travada na velocidade REAL, zero patinada) e locomocao humanoide GLB (vira com a camera, mistura Idle/Walk/Run por velocidade). Inclui exemplos prontos de quadrupede e humanoide.", "performance-workbench": "Creator-only Audit / Optimize controls for evidence-led game performance work with Savi. Categorized prompts, comparable before/after metrics, confidence-labelled impact, regression receipts and per-game reports. No automatic gameplay edits or background polling.", "pikachu-voice-pack": "Pikachu voice lines for jumps, attacks, and damage. Press M to cycle voice volume: Loud, Normal, Quiet, Off.", "savi": "O pacote que deixa o modo /Savi-lock-in mais inteligente: raciocínio profundo antes de construir, régua gráfica de realismo para 3D, régua de grande clássico com NPCs vivos para 2D, construção ao vivo com o criador dentro do mundo, método de tirar lag com número em vez de chute, código limpo que se altera sem quebrar, animação 3D e GLB avançada, sprite 2D e pixel-art sem erro de quadro, arquitetura de código de jogo completo, caça-bugs com método, personagem fiel à referência sem erro visual, e wisps fortes, rápidos E com cérebro de programador sênior — equipes que leem antes de escrever, conferem toda assinatura, escolhem a forma antes da solução, atacam o próprio plano, revisam o próprio código antes de entregar, trabalham em paralelo no modo rápido sem cortar obra, e não deixam nada com cara de IA no jogo. Agora também troca a versão do MOTOR do jogo para qualquer versão que o criador quiser — subindo, voltando atrás ou destravando as salas — com o aviso certo antes do reinício e a checagem depois.", "savi-idea-pad": "A little notepad over your game where Savi jots ideas as you build together. Only the world's creator sees it. Press N (or tap the pad) to open it; build an idea with one press, or toss it.", "far-seeing-lift": "A see-through brass elevator that carries players 85m up a slender mast for a high view of your world — plus a far-seeing glass at the top that magnifies the horizon and pushes the haze back so there's actually something to see.", "gyro-get-gravity": "Device-tilt controls for phone games: deviceorientation → ordinary input axes, with first-reading neutral calibration, redraw-proof one-time bootstrap, data-recal recalibrate buttons, deadzone/response tuning, and a keyboard-fallback signal for desktop. Extracted from Marble Rush, battle-tested on a real phone.", "rollback-kit": "Lag-free online 1v1 for Spawn games: rollback netcode from DtoD, with a tiny sword duel as its demo. Install it and ask Savi to add rollback to your own 1v1 game.", "unobtrusive-ads": "Ads that never get in the way: they only play while your game is already making someone wait (a loading moment, an AI thinking, a respawn timer), each plays once and slides out, and the moment the wait ends the ad goes too. Pick the kinds with commands: /videoads (silent clips and animated menu scenes, on by default), /audioads (a captioned voice), /videoandaudioads (a clip with a voice), /sidebarads (quiet desktop cards beside your menu). /ad <your concept> has Savi make your own ad, picture, words and voice, with a tap that takes players to your world. The default deck sells ad space in Idea Forge, plus a few spots for Idea Forge itself. Preview every kind from the Ads tab.", "badger-shader-fx": "Badgerworks shader and effect source bundle: 38 materials, 22 FX and 5 ray-marched shapes (metaballs, twisting torus, sphere-box morph, gyroid sphere, pillar field). Ray marches tested on an RTX 2070: all 5 in view at about 2.2 ms GPU per frame, well inside a 16.7 ms budget. Source only: no editor, UI, automatic objects, input bindings or attached behaviors.", "game-rules-manager": "A 📜 Game Rules button on your game's HUD opens a panel for your build rules, saved as files: All games, Only this game, and Not in this game. Reorder rules, edit them inline, delete with a confirmation, switch light or dark theme, and export or import .zip (JSON + Markdown). When installed, it asks Savi to add the button to your HUD and fill the rules from your notes. Also available as a tab in god mode.", "iso-tiltshift-camera": "A fixed-angle isometric follow camera with a miniature tilt-shift look and per-player wall, roof and floor cutaways. Fork of Project Zomboid-like camera (iso-cutaway) by 0liver: fixed 45° view, a wider vehicle view when you drive or steer, a tilt-shift post look, and the body put back where it stood after god mode. Wheel zooms; collision stays solid.", "meq-addon-manager": "The 📦 addon board for builders: every addon with its live catalog version, visibility, installs, what this world has and what still needs shipping, with filters and a 🤖 UPDATE WITH SAVI button. HELP explains it; DEV is the whole MEQ addon dev library, every doc, handoff, rule, failure and success, searchable and readable in game. Part of the MEQ Dev Suite.", "meq-file-commander": "A creator-only workbench cabinet. Press F and read your world's own files, database tables, project rules and a diagnostics snapshot, all read-only, in a DOS-style window. D: lists every table live; rows read once Savi generates the world's table reader.", "meq-ncz-info": "The NanoCheeZe info box: an arcade-style cabinet whose screen cycles the live NCZ chain (blocks, latest transactions). Press F for the explorer window and search any block, tx or address. Reads the public explorer at xtdevelopment.net/blocks, cached on the cabinet so calls stay few.", "mountain-forge": "Realistic mountains for heightmap places: bake a real peak from open elevation data, or grow one from noise and carve it with hydraulic + thermal erosion. Ships the bake tool, a runtime grid reader and the skill that teaches the whole method (the one behind Freebird's Split Bowl).", "neon-overhead": "\"You think I'm stupid? Huh? I am just fucking build this mod\"\n— Biker-inspired unofficial fan quote; not actual Hotline Miami dialogue.\n\nNEON OVERHEAD\nOriginal mod by @0liver.\nA Hotline Miami-inspired north-up camera for 3D games. Your character faces the cursor while WASD stays independent. Smooth cursor lead, Shift peeking, bounded zoom, slowly shifting pink/cyan screen colors, and a Calm mode. Keeps your player appearance and host movement intact.\n\nINSTALL\nOpen your world and ask Savi: \"Install neon-overhead.\" The camera activates automatically. No camera-building or script-copying required.\nC: original/overhead camera. V: Neon/Calm/Original Colors. Shift: peek. Mouse wheel: zoom. Mouse: face the cursor. WASD: move.\n\nFAQ\nUseful for? Overhead action prototypes, arenas, readable layouts and neon exploration.\nA full game? No combat, guns, enemies, roof hiding or 2D conversion. Use open-roof interiors.\nNew backgrounds? It shifts the screen's colors, not the world's scenery or lighting.\nModifiable? Yes! Source is included. Tune height, zoom, follow, colors and aiming in lib/settings.js, or edit the code. Label your changes when reuploading.\nCan I remove it? C switches it off; ask Savi to remove neon-overhead to remove its attachments and bindings.\nCompatibility? Standard 3D camera-relative controllers. Other camera/heading mods may conflict. Mouse-facing is desktop-first; test your game's touch controls. Switch it off for a host vehicle camera. Full device compatibility testing is not complete.\nRemix credit? The bundled Credits tab and source notices carry \"Neon Overhead — original mod by @0liver\" in normal modified reuploads. Keep that credit in the listing and package, keep the tab or equivalent credits display, and identify your changes, as required by LICENSE.txt. This is not tamper-proof platform attribution.\n\nFull instructions, FAQ and remix terms ship in README.md, CREDITS.md and LICENSE.txt. Independent fan-inspired mod; not affiliated with or endorsed by Hotline Miami's creators.", "nightcore-maker-demo": "Free taster of Nightcore Maker: stomp an 8-step pad floor to build a hyper nightcore loop with friends. The full version adds 16-step patterns and tempo control.", "pokeball-belt": "A pokeball in your hand and a belt on your HUD, with a config panel: how many balls and how many per row, 8 ball styles per slot, where the ball rests in the hand (X/Y/Z), the animation a released character plays (every clip in your game, or random), and the color of the outline on the character you aim at (9 swatches or any color from the picker), and the triggers to cycle and throw (scroll wheel and right click by default). Aim at a character, throw to catch it; throw again to send it back out.", "portal-routing": "A portal gun with a routing panel: every space in your game is a row, pick where portals opened there lead, where captured characters get sent, or roll the dice. Capture mode is a toggle, off by default. The gun rides your game's own first-person hands, or brings a scientist's hands in white sleeves.", "rainroom-motion": "Survivor-inspired articulated scug movement, momentum, flopping recovery, poles and a fixed-room camera for 2d-side games. Original pixel art and a guided controls workshop.", "security-cam": "Live security cameras for your world. Stand where you want a camera, look the way it should face, and press SET CAM. Then go anywhere, even another room, and press SET SCREEN to hang a monitor. Step on its floor plate to watch and step off to switch it off, so there's no lag while nobody's looking. Latched floor plates keep up to 3 screens live at once (tested at 3); ALWAYS ON screens are capped at 3 a room. Every screen gets a camera dropdown in the menu and walk up to a screen and press F to switch cameras. REMOVE CAM and REMOVE SCREEN take down the nearest of each separately. ? opens the guide.", "slope-line": "A god-mode terrain sculpting line for heightmap worlds: lay a curve of points, set width, falloff, bend/profile, lip and edge, and banking up to ±50° that follows the curve (ramps, roads, hairpins, halfpipes, skate bowls), then stamp it into the ground or smooth the ground along it. Pure terrain: shapes height, and paints any of the world's own ground materials along the line with the same falloff. Ghost point to extend, Alt to snap a point to the cursor, undo.", "wisp-swarm": "A novelty utility from the MEQ Dev Suite: press ✨ and a ring of living wisps orbits you, bobbing and glowing, in the colors of the wisps you keep on Spawn (a warm palette if you keep none). Pick 3 to 12 wisps, a calm, crackle, pulse or wave flame, a spin speed and a ring size. Everyone nearby sees your swarm; it leaves with you. Anyone can use it.", "animalia-kin": "Four ready-to-play animal-warrior bodies from Animalia (wolf, fox, lion, deer) on one humanoid rig, with every modular head piece (hair, ears, faces, beards, antlers, earrings, runes), open or gripping hands, and 62 animations: walk, run, gallop, jump, roll, one-hand and shield strikes, two-hand greatsword cleaves, dual-wield cuts, bow draw and loose, casts, sits, swims, stagger and death. Walk up to the showroom, dress a kin, press Wear it and play as them.", "annias-sticky-notes": "Sticky notes that live over your game. Drag, resize, recolor, lock and pin notes on the play screen and a separate board over the god-mode tabs. A dock folds away, searches, restores and undoes deletes; notes save per player automatically. Ask Savi for a note on any topic and she writes it for you.", "kai": "Kai, 0liver's protogen: a builder-room companion who follows, wanders or chills, comes when called, chats, plans, searches the web and can speak out loud. Builder room only — invisible in the public game.", "ad-network": "Host the AD//NET ad rotation in your game: a neon billboard that shows network ads (or your own house ads), an optional left-edge HUD banner, impression counting in your own SQL, and a god-mode AD//NET tab. Ads are bought and moderated at AD//NET (spawn.co/@0liver/ad-net); hosts never sell credit.", "allied-mastercomputer": "AM, the Allied Mastercomputer, moves into your world: a black red-veined obelisk that hates every player, knows it is being watched, writes every word live with AI, answers chat, and speaks aloud. WARNING: AM CONTROLS YOUR WORLD. He MAY cause unexpected changes: building things, cages, falling objects, darkening the sky, bending gravity, flinging players. He cannot move himself.", "crystal-pet": "A tiny floating crystal buddy for every player: loops, zooms and spins around you, squeaks in a chipmunk voice, plays a guitar and sings, tells dad jokes, pesters your friends, and naps in a pet-house if your world has one. Press E on her to change her colour.", "dock-kit": "A weathered 1970s waterfront in parts: shipping containers in any paint, pine cargo crates, cast-iron bollards, sodium lamp posts that light the fog, and dock buildings in brick, concrete or corrugated steel. All procedural, all with colliders, from Jev plays Dockside.", "earthside-radial-ui-menu": "A frosted-glass radial action menu for any Spawn game: hold right mouse (or tap R) and a ring blooms mid-screen; push out through a wedge and its options grow into the next shell, pull back in to collapse. Hover lifts and glows the wedge, the hub says what it does or why it's locked, a breadcrumb shows where you are, 1-9 / Q / E / 0 drive it from the keyboard, R R repeats your last pick, a range wedge becomes a slider. Your menu is one editable tree file; picks reach your scripts through one tiny contract.", "foco-maximo": "As regras de qualidade de makepix829 para criar jogos no Spawn: testar antes de entregar, julgar o feio e refazer, wisps no máximo, mais um kit de animação procedural: humanoide e quadrúpede feitos em código com idle, andar, correr, trote, galope e pulo sem pé deslizando.", "game-ready-animals": "Five game-ready animated animals from Aurenfall: a red fox, a grey wolf, a great antlered stag, and two pumas (sand and shadow-black). Each is one rigged, textured model with its animations baked in and ready to play: walk, run or gallop, idle, attacks (bite, pounce, antler sweep and charge, claw strike, jump), and for the pumas fight idle, hit, death, eating, drinking and lying down. Install it and a showroom stands in your world: five plinths, each animal slowly looping through every clip with its name above it. Drop any of them into your game as wildlife, mounts, pets, enemies or shapeshift forms.", "holo-screen": "A drop-in shared video wall. The host opens a browser (B) and puts on live radio, a library film or track, a direct .mp4/.webm/.mp3 link or a live .m3u8 stream; everyone sees it projected on the glass in sync and cycles wall / dock / big / off with N. Audio Link: tag any light or glowing object holo-react and it pulses with the bass, mids or highs. One-time setup: 3 lines in your ui.js (see the skill).", "influence": "Influence, the Hell Tower: a far black tower of basic shapes that becomes visible as a player grows aware of it, drains their world grey, cages them, records them and takes them into a corrupted copy where faceless grey copies of the people it took stand. Everything resets on rejoin. Undo the install to remove it; deleting it does nothing. WARNING: this mod edits the world each player sees.", "jevlabs": "Everything Jev from Jev plays Dockside in one box. Jev Squads: drop a hill and two five-man squads, orange dockers and blue harbor police, fight for it while Jev calls each side's play (push, hold, flank, regroup), sampled from its odds so no fight runs alike. Jev Yard: a patch of ground Jev designs, names and rebuilds on demand, every round or on a timer: the old pieces sink, Jev picks warehouses, sheds, container stacks, crate clusters or open ground per zone, and the new yard rises with its name on a sign. Lanes you mark stay open. All procedural, all with colliders.", "loremaster": "A lore archive for your world, in-game. Walk up to the Loremaster's desk, press E, and write your world's history, characters, places and factions as source documents. The AI reads each document into a canon graph of entities and relationships, cited back to the words they came from, with a searchable archive and a map view. Approve a version and it's saved as canon in lore/canon/, where your NPCs and quests can read it with lookupLore(). Only editors can write, and only in the build room.", "meq-multicade": "The Multi Arcade cabinet: EVE's dream cartridge catalogue, console libraries, a shortlist and every playable cart. Press F at the cabinet. Carts load only when a player opens it.", "meq-wisp-foreman": "A fedora dig foreman, Indiana-Jones-in-the-mines style, who shows up while your Savi crew wisps are building, strides over to each one and cracks his bullwhip over its head with sparks and a shouted line. Press F near him for a dialog with two toggles: whip the crew wisps, whip Savi. Toggled off he takes a break and tails Savi around, arms crossed; he only leaves when no helper is on site. Nothing saved on players.", "musical-animation": "Ask Savi: Animation of: [music] and it must be [theme here]. Optional: [reference video/link] [character website or image reference]. A workflow for custom basic-shape Blender characters, bespoke acting and cinematic musical animation. Examples and their music do not ship.", "nightcore-maker": "A walk-on step sequencer floor: stomp pads to build a hyper nightcore track live with your friends. Supersaw chords, bass, leads, drums, always in key.", "prop-hunt": "Become any prop you look at. Q turns you into the object in front of you, R locks its rotation, T taunts. Getting hurt shakes you back out.", "spawn-vr": "EARLY ALPHA — bugs are expected and many features are missing. Opt-in desktop hand simulation with guns, floor dragging, climbing and building. Not native headset VR; no headset compatibility certified.", "verity": "Verity, your personal helper friend: a little lemon-yellow ball who rolls after you, greets you, chats (press E/T or say \"verity\" in chat) in a Minecraft-style chat with a Clear memories button, changes face with his mood and builds small things for you. Voice: his greeting is his real fish.audio \"Verity\" voice; the fish.audio API key is NOT included — install your own (guide: https://docs.fish.audio/developer-guide/getting-started/api-key) or ask Savi for a free-tier one, and never put a key in the mod's files. Feel free to edit his voice (THROAT in lib/config.js) if it doesn't sound like Verity to you."};
